module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.changed_declaration_signature_consumer_unplanned

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data changed_declaration_signature_consumer_unplanned: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "changed_declaration_signature_consumer_unplanned" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "2026-10-09, PR #13607 bringup: runner_microvm_network_observe had been replaced by per-attempt sanitation helpers while ci_spec still named its removed runner_microvm_network_observe_wet CLI. The reference is workflow data, outside the declaration-call population described below. Restoring the observer and moving sanitation into runner_microvm_network_sanitation_observe preserves both consumers; workspace_network_producer_witness_test imports the restored production observer so the focused suite prepares its closure. Remaining ceiling: admission must resolve every emitted workflow entry/function pair, including data-carried references, before the required gate accepts it. This repair restores the particular route without claiming that broader gate exists.",
    "**a declaration's INTERFACE changes -- a product field retyped, an alias re-branded, a function parameter or result retyped, a constructor payload changed, a declaration removed -- and the untouched modules that READ it stay outside the required floor's prepared subject, so main admits an importer that no longer typechecks** (THE INVALID STATE is a merged tree holding a module that refuses under Strict preparation while every required lane that ran on the merging change reported green. The floor prepares the gate closure plus what the diff names: the touched modules and their DEPENDENCY closure. A reader of the changed declaration is a REVERSE dependent with an empty diff, so no diff-keyed selector sees it and it is never prepared.)",

    "THE HARM is deferred and misattributed. The broken reader sits on main until some LATER, UNRELATED change happens to pull it into its own subject -- and that change's author is the one who meets the refusal, in a file they did not touch, caused by a change they did not make. Every PR in between merges over a red it cannot see. It is the ordinary compiler floor (DESIGN section 4b: values inhabit declared types, fields exist) failing silently on the merge path, which is a below-baseline regression, not a missing differentiator.",

    "SPECIMEN (2026-09-23 side-chat ruling, review of gunbc#12120). 99c2d33263 (gunbc#11751, 2026-09-21) changed `gunbc.runner_microvm_network` `HelperStanding`'s four surface fields from `Int` to `HelperSurfaceReading` and introduced `ConvergeGeneration`, a `NonEmptyStr` brand, where the generation had been an `Int`. `dag/test/claim/runner/runner_microvm_lifecycle_witness_test.dag` still built them from `Int` literals, so it went invalid at that commit and never had a diff. ff2110b7e24 (gunbc#12002) then touched the same module, and its floor subject (run 35668300140: `touched-entry-compile-subject seeds=11`, exactly its touched files) left the witness out as well. It became visible only when gunbc#12077, an unrelated change, pulled it in, and gunbc#12120 repaired it. THE ATTRIBUTION IS CORRECTED HERE, NOT INHERITED: #12120 and the ruling name #12002 as the change, but at 7f10b25e (#12002's parent) the module already carries `HelperSurfaceReading` and `type ConvergeGeneration`, and at dcd1552e (#11751's parent) it carries neither. The class is unchanged by the correction, and it strengthens the harm: TWO merges' floors passed over the same broken reader. DETECTION WAS ACCIDENTAL: nothing was aimed at the reader. It was found because a later subject happened to include it.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, and the neighbours this is not. The reader has NO DIFF. The declaration's module has one, and it prepares GREEN, because the declaration is internally consistent. The refusal exists only at the reader, so a subject built from the touched set plus its dependencies is correct about everything it contains and blind to the one module that matters. [[check_reachable_only_from_an_entry_point_the_context_never_calls]] had the same shape for ONE interface component, a coproduct's arm set under an exhaustive match (gunbc#11194). Its dependents half, the seed ground `SeedArmSetChangedMatchConsumer`, was the PARTIAL AUTHORITY for this class: it planned match-bearing readers of a changed arm set and nothing else, not product-field types, parameters, results, constructor payloads or branded aliases. So the #11751 reader was out of reach by construction. The arm-set half was not wrong; it was one component of an interface treated as the whole.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below 1 on the merge path. The checker was real and refused the reader when invoked, but the required path did not invoke it on the live subject, and the only detection was accidental. CEILING 2, mechanically preventable: whether a reader typechecks against a changed interface is decidable, and the refusal already exists in Strict preparation. What was missing was a PLANNED subject that contains the reader. Rung 3 would need the merge path to typecheck the whole reverse closure of every change by construction rather than by selection. That is the whole-corpus floor and a cost question, not a missing fact.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: derive every changed declaration interface between the floor's own diff base and head, and seed its ACTUAL READER POPULATION into Strict preparation. The population comes from the declaration/reference index, not every importer, and it is closed through intermediate declarations only where their own INTERFACE references a changed one. LANDED WITH THIS ROW: `v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed` `SeedDeclarationInterfaceChangedConsumer` CONSOLIDATES the arm-set ground rather than forking a second mechanism. An arm-set change is one `InterfaceChangeGround` beside `SignatureChanged`, `DeclarationRemoved` and `PropagatedThrough`, realized by the host's `namespace_baseline` `interface_changed_consumers`. The receipt is the `[floor-phase] phase=interface-changed-consumers` line and one `[floor-plan] SeedDeclarationInterfaceChangedConsumer` line per changed declaration, naming its ground and the readers it added. The executed reds are in `required_floor_runner`: a product-field retype and a re-branded alias under an unchanged product each plan their untouched constructor, and it refuses when prepared. A retyped function parameter plans its caller and NOT an importer that never reads it. A body-only change plans nobody. Preparing only the touched module over the specimen's shape is GREEN, which is this row's latent failure reproduced: remove the ground and it returns. ON THE REAL HISTORY: the selector run over the specimen's own window (dcd1552e..99c2d332) plans `gunbc.test.claim.runner.runner_microvm_lifecycle_witness_test` among its readers, on a `SignatureChanged` of `HelperStanding`. TWO GROUNDS PLAN LESS THAN EVERY READER, and each is a measured correction rather than a preference. First, a coproduct that only GREW (`ArmSetGrown`: no arm removed, no surviving payload changed, and the residual interface outside the arms -- name and generic parameters -- unchanged) can stale only an exhaustive match, so it plans match readers alone, which is #11194's original population; an added arm beside an arity change is not growth and plans every reader. Second, an `admit_callers:` roster is not interface text, and its transitions are decided on presence first: absent to present (`AdmissionIntroduced`) plans every reader the roster does not name; present to absent and present to larger plan nobody; present to smaller (`AdmittedCallersNarrowed`) plans only the dropped callers. Refinement predicates carry no source span, so they are serialized canonically -- every literal kind, argument position and nesting -- and a numeric bound such as `range(max: 6)` to `range(max: 5)` is an interface change. On the specimen's window, treating a three-entry growth of `extdeps.exec.command` `argv_command`'s roster as a signature change planned 72 modules. Counting arm growth as a change to every reader planned 34. The two corrections leave 11.",

    "THE BOUND, STATED SO THE GREEN IS NOT OVER-READ. Four limits. (1) A reader outside the floor's source roots, such as a `src/v1` `.dag` mirror, is planned and COUNTED, not prepared. (2) A read through the flat bare channel is planned from the parser's own type occurrences, match-arm heads and CALL occurrences (a bare call with no import is the compiler's global-bare lookup of a unique top-level fn, found by the side-chat review of this repair), and VALUE occurrences -- the parser's expression-variable references, minus any an in-scope binder shadows, so a function passed as a value and a `data` read are one channel (both found by the side-chat review of this repair); counted apart, and PROPAGATES like a resolved one when it sits in an interface, so A -> B (flat) -> C plans C. An UNRESOLVED name occurrence from the tree walk plans nothing, because that walk also collects binders and labels. (3) A reader that reaches the changed declaration only through an INFERRED type, where no declaration on the path spells it or spells an interface that propagates it, is not reached. A function RETURNING the changed type does spell it, so its callers are reached through propagation. That is the grain of the reference index, and its trigger is the resolver's own reference relation replacing name occurrences as the consumer source. (4) A formatting-only edit inside a signature reads as a change and over-plans its readers: bounded by the reader relation, never widened to every importer. The rung holds where the floor runs, which is the required lane: `witnesses.yml`'s aggregate `witnesses` job needs `floor` on every pull-request head and every merge_group revision.",
    "RECEIPT 2026-09-28, THE LATENT POPULATION MEASURED WHOLE. The List de-fork (gunbc#12526) widened the required floor's planned module pool, and the widened pool refused 100 rows in 28 files that were already refusing on main, with no change from #12526 involved. Attribution by clever-heron-784 was an identity diff at file:line:col + diagnostic, comparing whole-corpus `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --repository gunbc --measured-root-demands tools/whole_corpus_compile_measured_root_demands.json --target dag` at control 6a58936 against the floor at head bae39e0. Of the 100 rows, 58 were an Optional<X> passed where X is declared, from the .first()/index-returns-Optional family, and 26 were bare-name ambiguity. The ambiguous names were render x17 (std.layout vs gunbc.demo.semantic_system_readout), json_string x7 (extdeps.languages.json.emit vs gunbc.required_lane_resolution_census) and settle x2 (gunbc.idea_pr_spine vs a test-local helper). The remaining 16 were: 1 unwired history argument; 4 InterfaceObservation rows resolving between two unrelated declarations (extdeps.netplan.netplan vs gunbc.runner_host_first_boot_receipt); a single-arm sum spelled `= Name`, which parses as an alias, so its variant was unresolved; a List<GrantIssue> matched as one GrantIssue, which the checker located at std.algebra FreeMonoid rather than at the match; a host String handed to a FreeMonoid<Char> parameter without the chars unfold; and six ConvergeVerdict rows where the variant name Absent collides with Optional's Absent. Renaming that variant plans every bare-Absent reader. That reaches further latent ambiguous reads (Unit x5, String x3, Filesystem x1), so those six rows are deferred to a follow-up that lands after the std.string_type String retirement, and this repair carries 94. Every row passed the scoped floor that planned it out and was refused by whole-corpus. That is this class seen from the population side: the reader was never unplanned by a SIGNATURE change. It was unplanned from the start and stayed broken until a pool change planned it. Repaired at each owning link by silent-ant-828, with the whole-corpus compile named above as the census, base against head: the 94 gone by identity, 0 new.",

    "WHAT THE REPAIR ADDS: THE FIX HAS TO BE CHECKED BY THE FLOOR TOO, NOT ONLY BY WHOLE-CORPUS. The first repair of the 26 ambiguity rows added an `import` to five importless files. Whole-corpus went clean. A claim_batch run over the same files then refused all five with UnimportedBareProvider: once a file declares an import, every OTHER bare name in it has to be imported too. So whole-corpus admitted a repair that the floor refuses, which is the same divergence in the opposite direction. The repair instead qualifies each ambiguous call by containment path (`std.layout.render(...)`) and leaves the file off the import channel. The receipt that caught this was a claim run over the repaired files, not a second compile.",

    "A SECOND ENTRY PATH THE TRIGGER DOES NOT REACH: A CHECKER CHANGE STRANDS READERS WITHOUT ANY INTERFACE CHANGE. The largest family in the latent population, an Optional<X> passed where X is declared, was not produced by a declaration changing. `.first()` has returned Optional since gunbc#4606. The readers were stranded when gunbc#11720 made the checker refuse an Optional at a Required position: a rule of the compiler changed, and no declaration any reader spells changed with it. The interface-change planner named in the trigger derives its seeds from changed declarations, so a change of this kind seeds nothing, and the strict refusal it introduces is census-checked only over the population that change itself prepares. #11720 fixed 94 sites inside that population; the rest waited for the next widening. Independently measured 2026-09-28 by quick-gull-795 on #12381 floor run 36422057907 (per-entry compiles at main 5bf2b13fb8: 24 of 34 files refusing) before gunbc#12572 landed the same repairs. For a change to a CHECKER, the reader population is every module the tightened rule can reach, not the readers of a declaration, so the whole-corpus prepared subject the ceiling names is the only planned subject that contains it.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed", decl_name: "InterfaceChangeGround", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed", decl_name: "interface_change_propagates", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed", decl_name: "interface_reader_population", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed_test", decl_name: "only_an_interface_read_propagates_a_change", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed_test", decl_name: "only_growth_and_a_narrowed_roster_plan_less_than_every_reader", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
